\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Dn On Suspected Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Flat   \b0\par\par\uc2 416 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2007\par 15:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.79      +0.09 \par  7.99% 2017 Bond   7.89%      Unchanged \par  Call Rate         8.00%      +215BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  October           0.29        -0.06 \par  *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee fell to its lowest closing level against the dollar in more than a month Monday as shrinking foreign fund inflows and suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  accentuated its weakness, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR39.79, up from INR39.70 at Friday's close.   \par \par \uc2 According to the head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at a private bank, the Reserve Bank of India bought dollars through state-run banks as it wants to stop the rupee from appreciating sharply.   \par \par \uc2 "They (the RBI) want to push the dollar/rupee up, and now is the right time to do so since the inflows are a bit tight," he said.   \par \par \uc2 After foreign fund inflows surged for months, the trend is now showing signs of a reversal as the country's stock market recently has wavered along with other markets on fears of a global rout driven by the U.S. subprime mortgage crisis.   \par \par \uc2 Latest data from the Securities and Exchange Board of India showed that foreign funds sold a net $1.15 billion of Indian stocks so far in November, as against net purchases of $5.07 billion in October, when the benchmark Sensex crossed 20,000 points for the first time.   \par \par \uc2 Riding on strong foreign fund flows, the rupee has gained over 11% against the dollar since January.   \par \par \uc2 "The country's finance minister and trade minister have voiced concerns about the rupee's gains hurting exporters and the RBI will surely want to keep the rupee weak," the private bank official said.   \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, prices stayed in narrow range as players awaited more clarity on how the liquidity situation will pan out.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.99% 2017 bond ended nearly unchanged at INR100.64 versus INR100.63 at Friday's close. Its yield was steady at 7.89%.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is unlikely to change its course any time soon and will remain rangebound as there isn't much to look forward to," said a bond trader with a primary dealership.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Vipin V. Nair; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; vipin.nair@dowjones.com \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 26-11-07 1424GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071126e3bq000qr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
