\par\par \b \uc2 Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says bought $11.9 bln in Sept   \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2007\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 13 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record $11.87 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September to slow the rupee's rise after U.S. rate cuts drew huge inflows into the stock market, its monthly bulletin showed on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India has bought $51.8 billion in the first nine months of 2007, with the previous record purchase at $11.86 billion in February.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the rupee has appreciated 12.3 percent against the dollar this year. It was trading at 39.4 rupees per dollar on Tuesday afternoon, after last week hitting 39.16 -- its strongest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign portfolio flows of nearly $17 billion into the stock market this year have been a key driver for the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have also risen $89.3 billion this year to $266.5 billion on Nov. 2. (Reporting by Anurag Joshi; Editing by Ranjit Gangadharan)   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/ \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071113e3bd001ai\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
