\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases on worries of capital outflows   \b0\par\par\uc2 318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2007\par 08:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped to its lowest close in two weeks on Tuesday, tracking losses in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors pared holdings in emerging markets on concerns about the fallout from the U.S. subprime crisis.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.42/43 per dollar, moving down from Monday's close of 39.36/37. It hit a near decade high of 39.16 last week.   \par \par \uc2 "There are no real inflows at the moment, but there were outflows, and the market is positioning for more funds to go out," said a senior dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 India's main stock index <.BSESN> snapped a six-day fall on Tuesday, ending its longest losing streak in nearly five years.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds have sold $438 million of local shares in November, trimming their net buys to just under $17 billion in 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Overseas investments into local equities have been a key driver of the rupee, which has gained more than 12 percent this year.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought a record $11.86 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in September to slow the rupee's rise after U.S. rate cuts drew huge inflows into the stock market.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely seen as playing an active role in tempering the rupee's ascent in October and November as well.   \par \par \uc2 Most dealers expect the rupee to trade in a broad 39.30-39.50 range this week.   \par \par \uc2 "Until we break out of this range, we're not going to get any clear direction," said the chief dealer with a foreign bank.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by C.J. Kurrien; Editing by Mark Williams)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071116e3bd001dp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
