\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee eases on oil buying,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  fears   \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2007\par 11:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rupee eased on Thursday as oil companies bought dollars and as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed on sentiment, but trading was muted ahead of a public holiday, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 After market hours on Wednesday, the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the limit for issuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds had been raised to 2.5 trillion rupees ($63.6 billion) from 2 trillion rupees.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.325/335 per dollar, lower from 39.30/31 at the close on Wednesday, when it hit 39.16 -- its strongest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 Markets will be closed on Friday for a public holiday.   \par \par \uc2 "Many companies were closed today for Diwali, and there wasn't much happening for most of the day," said a senior dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "Apart from some initial jitters, the market seems to have brushed off the increased MSS ceiling," said the dealer, referring to the so-called Market Stabilisation Scheme bonds.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $40 billion in the first eight months of 2007, and is widely suspected of having played an active role in tempering the rupee's ascent in recent months.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained about 12.5 percent against the dollar this year, powered by massive capital inflows, many slated for the record-setting stock market.   \par \par \uc2 India's benchmark share index <.BSESN> ended lower on Thursday though, extending losses into a fourth day, as credit jitters roiled global markets.   \par \par \uc2 Still, losses in the rupee were limited as exporters sold dollars, fearing further erosion in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar teetered close to its all-time lows against the euro, as the market waited to see whether the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would voice concern about the sharp rally in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by C.J. Kurrien; Editing by Mark Williams)   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071111e3b80007d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
