\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2 's cbank raises  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bond ceiling   \b0\par\par\uc2 161 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2007\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday raised the ceiling on bonds sold under the Market Stabilisation Scheme to 2.5 trillion ($63.6 billion) to drain surplus cash generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India said in a statement the threshold at which the ceiling would be reviewed in future would now be 2.35 trillion rupees.   \par \par \uc2 "With the MSS auction of treasury bills held today, the MSS outstanding will be 1.8 trillion rupees as on Nov. 8, " the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement said.   \par \par \uc2 The MSS bond ceiling has been raised three times in 2007 -- most recently in October.   \par \par \uc2 But inflows have remained robust, thanks to a U.S. rate cut and a booming local stock market, pushing the rupee to near-decade highs.   \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Anurag Joshi, Editing by Mark Williams)   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/MSS   (URGENT)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071110e3b70009u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
