\par\par \b \uc2 FACTBOX- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  raises  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bond ceiling   \b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 November 2007\par 15:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 Nov 7 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's capacity for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday by increasing the ceiling on the amount of market stabilisation scheme bonds it can issue to 2.5 trillion rupees ($63.6 billion) from 2 trillion.   \par \par \uc2 For a story, please see [ID:nBOM27231].   \par \par \uc2 Here are five facts about bonds and bills issued under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Market Stabilisation Scheme (MSS): --------------------------------------------------------------- * Huge capital inflows have pushed the rupee to its strongest level against the dollar in nearly a decade, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to contain it by buying dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Latest data shows it bought nearly $40 billion in the first eight months of 2007. * Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  releases rupees into the money market, which could be inflationary if left in circulation. MSS debt, which was introduced in April 2004, is sold to absorb the surplus funds in a process called sterilisation. * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows outstanding issuance will be 1.8 trillion rupees as on Nov. 8. * The government has to pay interest on the MSS debt, so it meets with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to decide if the ceiling on issues needs to be changed once sales hit a pre-determined threshold. * Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed selling MSS bonds in March, after a gap of 18 months, the ceiling has now been increased five times by a total of 1.7 trillion rupees.   \par \par \uc2 It was raised by 150 billion rupees twice in April, by 400 billion rupees in August, 500 billion rupees in October and now another 500 billion rupees on Nov. 7. Source: Reuters, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site (  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbi.org.in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbi.org.in  }}}\uc2 ) ($1=39.3 rupees)   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/MSS (FACTBOX)|LANGEN|SNI|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071107e3b7001ld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
