\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  rupee steady after cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -dealers   \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2007\par 10:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2   (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Nov 6 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was blocked from hitting a near-decade high on Tuesday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars through the day to ensure the local unit ended steady, absorbing strong portfolio-related capital inflows, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2  The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 39.305/320 per dollar, a shade higher than Monday's close of 39.31/32 when it hit 39.22 -- its strongest since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2  "With the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  squatting there throughout the day, the market was unable to drive up the rupee," said a senior dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2  Sentiment on the rupee continued to be buoyant after Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram said on Monday that it was likely to appreciate further due to strong economic growth. [ID:nBOM339728].   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that exporters trimmed dollar holdings, anticipating further erosion in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.   \par \par \uc2  India's benchmark share index <.BSESN> ended lower on Tuesday, but the outlook for overseas investments into local shares remains buoyant, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2  Foreigners have poured in more than $17 billion so far this year into local shares -- a key driver for the rupee's rally -- well above a full-year record of $10.7 billion in 2005.   \par \par \uc2  But with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  playing an active role in tempering the rupee's rise, dealers remained cautious about taking large positions in the local unit.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $40 billion in the first eight months of 2007, and Swiss bank UBS estimates it bought a record $16 billion in September, in a bid to slow the rupee's rise.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/(UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071109e3b6001cl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
