\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  may have to raise  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bond cap -DBS\b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2007\par 06:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Nov 6 (Reuters) - Indian policymakers may have to raise more bonds sold under the Market Stabilisation Scheme (MSS) to drain surplus cash generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , DBS said in a research note on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The MSS bond ceiling has been raised three times in 2007 -- latest in October. The outstanding issuance was around 1.74 trillion rupees below a self-imposed ceiling of 2 trillion rupees. It is reviewed if the outstanding hits 1.85 trillion.\par \par \uc2 But inflows have remained robust, thanks to a U.S. rate cut, and a booming local stock market, pushing the local unit to near-decade highs, and DBS expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep up with its rupee selling tactics for the remainder of the year.\par \par \uc2 "Assuming capital flows revert to normal patterns, we would still expect $3-4 billion monthly net surplus in the coming months, and by extension dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of similar amounts," Ramya Suryanarayanan, the analyst at the bank wrote.\par \par \uc2 "Bonds outstanding under MSS should reach $44 billion by early November and should hit $46-47 billion sometime in November or December, we reckon," it said.\par \par \uc2 "The sterilisation, however, should prove insufficient," it said.\par \par \uc2 Authorities may resort to capital controls if they are unable to stem the flood of money, but the measures are unlikely to be draconian in nature as India needs huge amounts of money to fund its infrastructure needs, the Singapore-based bank said. (Reporting by Saikat Chatterjee, editing by Harish Nambiar) \par \par \uc2 INDIA-BONDS/DBS|LANGEN|SNI|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071106e3b6000bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
