\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee in sight of 9-\u189\'00\'BD yr high on inflows   \b0\par\par\uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2007\par 04:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed towards its highest in more than 9-\u189\'00\'BD years on Monday as dealers bet overseas funds would pour into record-breaking shares and as the dollar plumbed record lows against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m.(0415 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 39.355/365 , not far from its most recent 9-\u189\'00\'BD year high of 39.27, and climbing from the previous finish of 39.445/455.   \par \par \uc2 "The cues are all very positive for the rupee, and it's just a question of time before it hits a new high," said the chief dealer with a corporate.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the flows into the stock market were expected to be strong, which would lift the rupee. Overseas buying of local shares have been a key driver of the rupee, which has gained more than 12 percent this year.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark share index <.BSESN> surged 3 percent to a record high in opening trades on Monday, after gaining 9.6 percent last week. It has now risen more than 25 percent, and hit record highs in 21 of 28 sessions, since the U.S. Federal Reserve cut interest rates on Sept. 18.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed foreign funds were net buyers of $53 million of shares on Thursday, taking their net investment to $17.1 billion so far this year -- well above the full-year record inflow of $10.7 billion in 2005.   \par \par \uc2 Of that, almost $8 billion has come since the Fed rate cut.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee was also boosted after the dollar hit a record low against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on widespread speculation that the Federal Reserve will cut rates again on Wednesday. Still, gains in the rupee were moderated by importer demand for dollars and dealers expected some sporadic \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit gains.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $40 billion in the first eight months of the year in a bid to stem the rupee's ascent, and traders said it has been active in September and October as well.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/(UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071101e3at0009s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
