\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases as cbank, record oil weigh   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Anurag Joshi   \par \uc2 338 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2007\par 05:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 16 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee retreated from 9-1/2-year highs on Tuesday, after record oil prices raised concerns of a wider trade deficit and traders suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee ended at 39.345/360 per dollar, weaker than Monday's close of 39.305/310. Last week, it had hit 39.27 -- its strongest level since March 1998.   \par \par \uc2 Crude <CLc1> rose to record near $88 a barrel. Oil is India's biggest import and analysts are concerned that the spike could deteriorate the trade deficit, which was $32.5 billion in the first five months of the fiscal year that began in April.   \par \par \uc2 "In the first five months of this fiscal year, the trade deficit has widened by some 60 percent on the back of rising oil prices, as well as brisk growth in non-oil imports," Standard Chartered said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has been the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia, rising by about 12.5 percent this year, despite aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has bought $39.9 billion in the first eight months of 2007.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI bought dollars off and on to not let the rupee rise past 39.30," a state-run bank trader said, adding that a few in the market fear that a correction in the stock market could put pressure on the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 The main stocks index <.BSESN> rose to a record high for the 18th time in 19 sessions on Tuesday, but gave up the day's gains as investors were concerned about expensive valuations.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign funds bought $957 million of local equities on Monday, taking the total inflow this month to $4.6 billion.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071019e3ag0004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
