\par\par \b \uc2 Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says bought $1.8 bln in August   \b0\par\par\uc2 282 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Oktober 2007\par 14:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $1.82 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in August, its monthly bulletin showed on Friday, the smallest monthly purchase this year as it was when the subprime crisis had knocked the rupee to four-month lows.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India has bought $39.9 billion over the first eight months of 2007, including more than $11 billion in both February and July, trying to contain the rupee.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not as necessary in August because the rupee <INR=IN> weakened beyond 41 per dollar as the U.S. subprime crisis roiled global markets, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its uptrend towards the end of that month.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been active in September and October as the rupee extended its gains to more than 12.5 percent against the dollar this year, the most of any Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . On Thursday it hit a 9-\u189\'00\'BD year high of 39.27 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 A key factor in the rupee's rise has been foreign buying of stocks, but foreigners were net sellers of $1.9 billion in August as fears of a global credit crunch hit investor appetite for emerging market assets.   \par \par \uc2 Net foreign buying of stocks has since recovered to reach $16.5 billion so far this year, including almost $3.5 billion in October so far.   \par \par \uc2 Reflecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves have risen sharply this year. They were at $251.3 billion as at Oct. 5, up $75.1 billion so far in 2007.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071012e3ac00113\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
