\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia pauses as c.banks seek to cap peso, rupee   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Kevin Yao   \par \uc2 808 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2007\par 05:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Oct 11 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were range-bound on Thursday after strong gains in recent sessions, with investors trying to guess the direction of the dollar ahead of a meeting of Group of Seven finance chiefs next week.   \par \par \uc2 Fears of heightened \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by regional central banks kept some investors sidelined, as central banks in India and the Philippines were spotted trying to rein in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The high-yielding Philippine peso <PHP=> hit 44.05 per dollar, a seven-year high, but suspected dollar-buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept it away from the psychologically important 44 level.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always there to smooth volatility or prevent the peso from strengthening too much," said a trader in Manila, adding that the 44 level would be tested soon.   \par \par \uc2 But a second trader felt that level would hold until next week due to the presence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and profit-taking.   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=>, another high-yielder, steadied near 9,080 per dollar, down a fifth of a percent from late Asian trade on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has gained 3.3 percent since Sept. 18, when the U.S. Federal Reserve cut its benchmark interest rate by a hefty 50 basis points and sparked a rally in most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The peso has risen 4.3 percent versus the dollar since then.   \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar fell versus the euro <EUR=> amid speculation that the Fed may cut rates again this month.   \par \par \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  strategist Christy Tan said trading in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was subdued ahead of public holidays in some Asian countries, and investors were looking to the G7 meeting for comments that could set the tone for the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 "The market focus will be likely to switch to the upcoming G7 meeting next week, where European officials are expected to step up calls for China and Asia to share the burden of global imbalance adjustments," she said.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee <INR=IN>, Asia's best performer this year with gains of 12.6 percent, pulled back from its 9-1/2-year high of 39.275 per dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Official data showed \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves swelled by $18.9 billion in September, highlighting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to stem rupee gains fuelled by foreign funds.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=> hit a two-week low at 921.30 per dollar on reports Dutch  \uc2 Philips Electronics\uc2  had sold a stake in  \uc2 LG.Philips LCD.\uc2  As expected, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held interest rates steady on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hovered near 1.4640 to the U.S. dollar, off its 10-year peak of 1.4625 hit on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  surprised the market by tightening monetary policy slightly.   \par \par \uc2 Many analysts believe Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will tolerate long-term appreciation, but they caution that it could step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term to prevent any sharp rise now.   \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> eased as far as 3.382 per dollar, a day after it rose past 3.38 to a 9-1/2-year high.   \par \par \uc2 "The break below 3.3800 paves the way for testing the key level of 3.3500 last seen on Feb. 11, 1998," said Suresh Ramanathan, a strategist at CIMB Bank.   \par \par \uc2 "It's a big gap between 3.3800 and 3.3500, so we could see very choppy trades," he said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0740 GMT    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.29         117.25       -0.03\par  Sing dlr        1.4639         1.4647       +0.05\par  Taiwan dlr      32.580         32.591       +0.03\par  Korean won      916.90         916.10       -0.09\par  Baht             34.17          34.18       +0.03\par  Peso             43.98          44.15       +0.39\par  Rupiah         9080.00        9063.00       -0.19\par  Rupee            39.31          39.31       +0.01\par  Ringgit         3.3730         3.3740       +0.03\par  Yuan            7.5056         7.5115       +0.08\par  Change so far in 2007\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       117.29         119.01       +1.47\par  Sing dlr        1.4639         1.5337       +4.77\par  Taiwan dlr      32.580         32.585       +0.02\par  Korean won      916.90         929.50       +1.37\par  Baht             34.17          36.08       +5.59\par  Peso             43.98          49.03      +11.48\par  Rupiah         9080.00        8988.00       -1.01\par  Rupee            39.31          44.26      +12.59\par  Ringgit         3.3730         3.5270       +4.57\par  Yuan            7.5056         7.8051       