\par\par \b \uc2 India cbank in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  swaps to tame cash, rupee-traders   \b0\par\par\uc2 476 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2007\par 14:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Oct 11 (Reuters) - India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has begun doing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps with state banks to blunt some of the rupees it injects while buying dollars and to help exporters get a better exchange rate, dealers said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the spot market this year to slow down the rupee's ascent against the dollar, but this has flooded the market with excess cash that could fuel inflation.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has now started entering into swap deals with state banks -- by selling dollars in the spot market and buying them in the forward market, traders at five banks said.   \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman was not available for comment.   \par \par \uc2  The swap deals help the RBI to reduce some of the surplus rupees generated by its own \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while simultaneously raising the value of dollars in the forward market, enabling exporters to book their receivables at a higher margin.   \par \par \uc2  "It is a win-win situation for the RBI because it is not only preventing the rupee from rising sharply, but also keeps a check on system liquidity," a trader at a local bank said.   \par \par \uc2  The RBI has done an estimated $1-$1.5 billion worth of swap trades in two days with state-run banks and most of the forward deals were struck for December-March, traders said.   \par \par \uc2  "It's a third front in the battle against rising liquidity. First we had cash reserve ratio, then market stabilisation bonds and now this," said a senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a European bank.   \par \par \uc2  Six-month annualised forward premiums moved up to 1.75 percent on Thursday from 1.49 percent on Wednesday, while three-month forwards climbed to 1.61 percent from 1.52 percent.   \par \par \uc2  "It's a small relief for exporters as it will give them a better value for their exports but at the same time it points to a liquidity build-up in the future," an analyst at a private bank said.   \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the rupee <INR=IN> climbed to 39.27 per dollar -- its highest level since March 1998. It has risen 12.6 percent in 2007, making it the best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the dollar in Asia.   \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the ceiling for issuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds by a third to 2 trillion rupees ($50.9 billion) to boost its firepower.   \par \par \uc2  The bonds are used to drain rupee funds caused by the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The RBI bought $38.1 billion in the first seven months of 2007, according to latest data, and traders say the purchases have picked up in the last few weeks due to surging foreign portfolio flows in India's booming stock market.  ($1=39.3 rupees)       \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071011e3ab001j3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
