\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Bonds Down Ahead Of Auctions; Rupee Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 505 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Oktober 2007\par 14:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                     As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.44      -0.05 \par  7.99% 2017 Bond   7.93%      +2BPs \par  Call Rate         6.00%      Unchanged \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  September         0.39       -0.04 \par *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices fell Monday as a slew of new bond sales lined up for during the week damped demand in the secondary market, traders said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Speculation that India's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may soon act to absorb inflation-fueling excess cash in the banking system also held back investors from buying bonds, they said.   \par \par \uc2 The market's current lackluster mood is likely to continue in the coming sessions as traders await INR180 billion of scheduled sovereign bond auctions this week.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.99% 2017 bond ended at INR100.37, down from INR100.50 at Friday's close. Its yield rose two basis points.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is jittery that the RBI may do some more monetary tightening because of the excess liquidity in the system," said a bond dealer at a private bank. Another dealer said many market participants expect the Reserve Bank of India to hike banks' cash-to-deposit ratio to drain liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 In its efforts to keep a lid on banks' excess funds, the RBI has raised the cash reserve ratio three times this year. The CRR, which is the share of deposits banks must hold with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cash, is currently 7%.   \par \par \uc2 But K. Harihar, treasury head at  \uc2 Development Credit Bank\uc2 , said the RBI will likely stand pat in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 "I don't think the RBI will go for a CRR hike since the MSS bond cap has now been raised," Harihar said.   \par \par \uc2 The federal government last week raised the ceiling for bond sales under the market stabilization scheme to INR2 trillion for the current financial year from INR1.5 trillion previously.   \par \par \uc2 Under the scheme, the RBI sells bonds outside the federal government's normal borrowing calendar to absorb liquidity created by its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fiscal year runs from April to March.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee strengthened against the U.S. dollar despite a fall in local stocks triggering concerns about foreign fund outflows.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR39.44, down from INR39.49 at Friday's close.   \par \par \uc2 "Foreign fund flows were dominating again today despite the Sensex' fall, and the dollar would have fallen further but for the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the RBI," said a state-owned bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer.   \par \par \uc2 The Bombay Stock Exchange's 30-stock benchmark index Sensex lost 281.97 points, or 1.6%, to end the day at 17491.39.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar could fall to INR39.00 during the week if local stocks recover in coming sessions as foreign fund inflows surge, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Vipin V. Nair, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; vipin.nair@dowjones.com [ 08-10-07 1242GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020071008e3a8000v2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
