\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-FACTBOX- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  raises  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bond ceiling   \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2007\par 04:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats story from Thursday)   \par \par \uc2  Oct 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's capacity for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday by increasing the ceiling on the amount of market stabilisation scheme debt it can issue to 2 trillion rupees ($50.6 billion) from 1.5 trillion.   \par \par \uc2  For a related story, please see [ID:nMBI000634].   \par \par \uc2  Here are five facts about bonds and bills issued under the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Market Stabilisation Scheme (MSS):  ---------------------------------------------------------------    \par \par \uc2  * Huge capital inflows have pushed the rupee to its strongest level against the dollar in 9-\u189\'00\'BD   years, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to try to contain it by buying dollars. Latest data shows it bought $38.1 billion in the first seven months of 2007.   \par \par \uc2  * Such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  releases rupees into the money market, which could be inflationary if left in circulation. MSS debt, which was introduced in April 2004, is sold to absorb the surplus funds in a process called sterilisation.   \par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data shows outstanding issuance was around 1.18 billion rupees on Sept. 21. Since then the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has auctioned another 170 billion rupees of bonds.   \par \par \uc2  * The government has to pay interest on the MSS debt, so the government and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meet to decide if the ceiling on issues need to be changed once sales hit a pre-determined level.   \par \par \uc2  * Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed selling MSS bonds in March, after a gap of 18 months, the ceiling had already been increased three times by a total of 700 billion rupees. It was raised by 150 billion rupees twice in April and by 400 billion rupees in August.   \par \par \uc2  Source: Reuters, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site (  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.rbi.org.in"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.rbi.org.in  }}}\uc2 )  ($1=39.5 rupees)       \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/MSS (FACTBOX, REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071005e3a500034\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
