\par\par \b \uc2 INSTANT VIEW 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  raises  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bond ceiling   \b0\par\par\uc2 508 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2007\par 16:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds more comments)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday by increasing the ceiling on the amount of special bonds it can issue to absorb the rupees generated by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The limit on the bonds, known as market stabilisation bonds, was lifted to 2 trillion rupees ($50.6 billion) from 1.5 trillion, a statement for the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) said.   \par \par \uc2 Following are some quick comments from analysts.   \par \par \uc2 Latest...   \par \par \uc2 SHUBHADA RAO, CHIEF ECONOMIST,  \uc2 YES BANK\uc2 , MUMBAI:   \par \par \uc2 "It is absolutely in line with expectations. Probably even the CRR measure will be in the reckoning sometime soon, given the pace of inflows and the need for the RBI to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 ABHEEK BARUA, CHIEF ECONOMIST AT  \uc2 HDFC BANK\uc2 , NEW DELHI:   \par \par \uc2 "With this, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is saying that they will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  fairly aggressively and the rupee may even slip in the near term if capital inflows slows a bit.   \par \par \uc2 "With the government's borrowing programme frontloaded for the first three months of the second half of the year, it will have quite a draining effect on liquidity. I think the cash reserve ratio increase is put on the back burner at least for now.   \par \par \uc2 "They have enough ammunition for the moment."   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 HARISH MENON, ECONOMIST,  \uc2 ING VYSYA BANK\uc2 , MUMBAI:   \par \par \uc2 "Considering the scale at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, I don't think this hike in the MSS ceiling is sufficient. They will have to hike the ceiling at least one more time and this hike has kept alive the chances of a cash reserve requirement increase in the near term."   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 D.K. JOSHI, PRINCIPAL ECONOMIST, CRISIL, MUMBAI:   \par \par \uc2 "I think this measure will need to be complimented by CRR hike to deal with the deluge of capital flows.   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 Earlier...   \par \par \uc2 INDRANIL PAN, CHIEF ECONOMIST, KOTAK MAHINDRA BANK, MUMBAI:   \par \par \uc2 "We have been expecting a hike in MSS limit as the outstanding issues have already breached the threshold. Given the more than 500 billion rupees of liquidity in the system, it becomes inevitable for more MSS issuances. With the enhanced limit on MSS, any apprehension of increase in CRR could be pushed to a later date, possibly till the announcement of the policy."   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 A. PRASANNA, ANALYST, ICICI SECURITIES, MUMBAI:   \par \par \uc2 "It is more or less along expected lines. It looks like for sometime the RBI may not be using the CRR (cash reserve ratio) option, at least until the policy review."   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 MANOJ SWAIN, HEAD OF TRADING AT STANDARD CHARTERED BANK, MUMBAI:   \par \par \uc2 "This was broadly expected and markets should largely take it in their stride and bonds may start 0.05-0.07 rupees lower tomorrow. But with this, the cash reserve requirements increase is on the back burner until the policy meeting later this month as this has given them enough firepower until then."   \par \par \uc2 - - - - -   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CBANK/MSS (INSTANT VIEW, UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071007e3a40010e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
