\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee pushed off 9-1/2-yr peak by cbank-traders   \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2007\par 10:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 4 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee climbed to its strongest level against the dollar in 9-\u189\'00\'BD years on Thursday as foreigners continued to pour funds into the booming economy, but suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove it off its peak.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> rose just over 0.5 percent to 39.36 per dollar, its strongest level since March 1998, but closed at 39.49/50, above Wednesday's finish of 39.575/585.   \par \par \uc2 "Flows, flows, flows -- they just keep coming," said a senior dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that despite the benchmark share index <.BSESN> snapping an 11-day rally, overseas funds continued to invest heavily in Indian stocks, which boosted the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market, which had risen 15.1 percent in its 11-day run of gains, was briefely in positive territory in early deals but failed to sustain the momentum that had seen it hit a record high in each of the previous 10 sessions.   \par \par \uc2 Overseas investments into local stocks have been a keep driver of the rupee, that has gained about 12 percent this year, to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that some large exporters also pared their dollar holdings when the rupee broke 39.50, on concerns that the rupee was going to appreciate further in the near term.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee's rise was blocked by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $38.1 billion in the first seven months of 2007 in a bid to cap the rupee.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  will review a limit on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds if asked by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram said on Wednesday, and analysts said the ceiling would have to rise at least by a third to 2 trillion rupees ($50.5 billion) if the rupee's rise was to be checked.   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/MARCH (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071007e3a4000mi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
