\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 India central bank \highlight\uc2  arms for more rupee  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By V. Ramakrishnan and Saikat Chatterjee   \par \uc2 638 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2007\par 16:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Recasts with more analyst comment, background)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Oct 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's firepower to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, a move analysts said might check the pace of rupee gains near term and lower chances of monetary tightening before a month-end review.   \par \par \uc2 Strong capital inflows into the world's fastest-growing major economy after China have pushed up the rupee <INR=IN>, making it Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained more than 12 percent against the dollar since the start of January and reached a 9-1/2-year high of 39.36 per dollar on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars and selling rupees aggressively in recent days to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising too quickly but its selling has released inflation-fuelling spare rupees into the economy.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement after market hours that the amount of special bonds it can issue to absorb rupees generated by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been raised to 2 trillion rupees ($50.6 billion) from 1.5 trillion for this fiscal year to March.   \par \par \uc2 "With this, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is saying that they will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  fairly aggressively and the rupee may even slip in the near term if capital inflows slow a bit," said Abheek Barua, chief economist at  \uc2 HDFC Bank\uc2  in New Delhi.   \par \par \uc2 Barua said heavy government borrowing coming up could help drain excess cash from the system, which meant the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not need to raise banks' reserve requirements, or cash reserve ratio, just yet.   \par \par \uc2 But he did not rule out an increase at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next policy review on Oct. 30.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has increased banks' reserve requirements, the proportion of cash they have to park with it, by 200 basis points since December as another way of soaking up excess funds.   \par \par \uc2 "The cash reserve ratio increase is put on the back burner at least for now," Barua said. "They have enough ammunition for the moment."   \par \par \uc2 BIG CAPITAL FLOWS   \par \par \uc2 Market speculation had been rife that Indian authorities would either have to raise the limit on the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, known as market stabilisation bonds (MSS), or increase the cash reserve ratio from 7 percent to cope with a build-up of funds.   \par \par \uc2 They last raised the MSS limit in August but since the U.S. Federal Reserve cut interest rates on Sept. 18, the rupee has gained 2.6 percent and foreign portfolio investment into Indian stocks has surged by $4.9 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market hit 10 record highs in a row after the Fed's move and although the benchmark BSE index <.BSESN> snapped an 11-day rise on Thursday, analysts say appetite for Indian assets is unlikely to fade significantly.   \par \par \uc2 Some economists did not rule out a cash reserve ratio increase before Oct. 30. It too was last raised in August.   \par \par \uc2 "Considering the scale at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, I don't think this hike in the MSS ceiling is sufficient," said Harish Menon, economist at  \uc2 ING Vysya Bank\uc2  in Mumbai.   \par \par \uc2 "They will have to hike the ceiling at least one more time and this hike has kept alive the chances of a cash reserve requirement increase in the near term."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the new limit for the fiscal year 2007/08 would be reviewed if MSS bond issuance exceeded 1.85 trillion rupees.   \par \par \uc2 The outstanding balance of MSS bonds would be 1.45 trillion rupees on Oct. 5, it said. ($1=39.5 rupees)   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-ECONOMY/BONDS (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020071004e3a4001v9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
