\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  Rupee Falls On Suspected RBI  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 ; Bonds Tad Up   \b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2007\par 15:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.81      +0.09 \par  7.99% 2017 Bond   7.90%      Unchanged \par  Call Rate         8.75%      +155 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  September         0.38        -0.14 . \par *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee closed weaker against the dollar for the first time this week Friday, on concerns a dogged \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would step up dollar purchases, dealers said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar closed at INR39.81, up from its previous close of INR39.72.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the session and, coupled with demand from oil importers, the dollar was well supported," the chief dealer at a local bank said.   \par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee has gained more than 11% since the start of the year, as record breaking gains for local shares attract foreign investors. The dollar fell to INR39.62 Wednesday, its lowest level since April 1998, fueling concerns of a slowdown in local exports.   \par \par \uc2 India's trade deficit widened to $21.580 billion in the April-June quarter of the current financial year, from $16.946 billion in the year-earlier quarter, the Reserve Bank of India said Friday.   \par \par \uc2 India's financial year runs from April 1 to March 31.   \par \par \uc2 "Exports have shown good resilience so far but the pace of the rupee's appreciation could hurt growth going forward," said Rupa Rege Nitsure, chief economist at  \uc2 Bank of Baroda.\par \par \uc2 A stronger rupee poses the biggest downside risk to earnings of Indian software companies, JPMorgan Chase Bank said in a research note.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI has little choice but to conduct aggressive foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the rupee's gains," the note said.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI may have bought around a net $6 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the last two weeks, according to  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2 's estimates.   \par \par \uc2 In the government bond market, bond prices rose marginally as inflation remained benign, but volumes were lackluster on the last trading day of the Jul-Sep quarter.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.99% 2017-dated bond ended at INR100.57, up slightly from INR100.55 at the previous close.   \par \par \uc2 "The inflation data was positive but concerns of more bond sales next week kept prices in check," said Manoj Swain, head of fixed-income trading at Standard Chartered Bank.   \par \par \uc2 India's headline wholesale price index-based inflation rate eased to 3.23% in the week ended Sept. 15, from 3.32% a week earlier. A Dow Jones Newswires poll of five analysts had forecast an inflation rate of 3.41%.   \par \par \uc2 After market hours Friday, the RBI said it would sell INR70 billion of bonds under its market stabilization scheme next week.   \par \par \uc2 Under the scheme, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells bonds outside the federal government's regular market borrowing plan to keep a lid on excess liquidity in the banking system.   \par \par \uc2 -By Neelabh Chaturvedi, Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com [ 28-09-07 1318GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070928e39s001ha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
