\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee hits 9-yr high, cbank watched   \b0\par\par\uc2 284 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2007\par 04:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee touched a nine-year high on Thursday on positive Asian cues and expectations of robust investment flows, but dealers remained cautious about provoking the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m. (0415 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 39.66/67 per dollar, easing from an early high of 39.62, its strongest since April 1998, that was also tested on Wednesday before closing at 39.700/705.   \par \par \uc2 "The mood is still rupee bullish, but there are concerns that the stock market's rally may be a little overdone," said the chief dealer with a foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 India's benchmark share index <.BSESN> hit a seventh successive all-time high in early trade.   \par \par \uc2 Data showed foreign funds bought nearly $1.9 billion of Indian shares in the five days after last Tuesday's cut in U.S. interest rates, taking their net purchases in 2007 to $11.3 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee gained positive cues from other stock markets in Asia that hit record highs.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained more than 11.5 percent this year, aided by massive capital inflows, to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  loomed over the market. The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been widely seen selling rupees in a bid to quell its rise.   \par \par \uc2 The most recent data shows the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $38.1 billion in the first seven months of 2007 to slow the rupee's appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070930e39r00016\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
