\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rate swaps near 3-week high, wary of cbank   \b0\par\par\uc2 189 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2007\par 10:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 27 (Reuters) - Indian overnight indexed swaps hovered near three-week highs on Thursday on investors' wariness over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures to curb surplus cash in the banking system. At 2:15 p.m., the five-year overnight indexed swap was at 7.2550/7.2750 percent, slightly below a three-week high of 7.26/7.28 percent hit on Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 "Liquidity is certainly good and is expected to remain relatively easy given the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and we expect more steps to reduce liquidity," a dealer with a private sector bank said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 100 billion rupees worth of Market Stabilisation Bonds on Wednesday and is expected to announce more such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds in the coming days.   \par \par \uc2 Surplus cash in the banking system, as reflected by the daily reverse repo auction, increased to 281.80 billion rupees on Thursday, from 44.95 billion rupees on Monday. Dealers attributed the inflows to redemption, increased government spending and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -SWAPS|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070927e39r000ox\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
