\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rate swaps ease on cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  hopes   \b0\par\par\uc2 269 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2007\par 10:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 20 (Reuters) - Indian overnight indexed swaps eased on Thursday as traders expected aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market would raise cash levels in the banking system. At 1:30 p.m., the five-year overnight indexed swap was at 7.05/7.07 percent, a tad lower than 7.07/7.09 percent at the previous close.   \par \par \uc2 The Indian rupee strengthened past 40 per dollar on Thursday, for the first time in more than nine years, after lower U.S. rates brightened the outlook for high-yielding assets like the Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Expectations are strong that with a low inflation, the RBI will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rupee's rise," a foreign bank trader said.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) bought $11.4 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July, taking its dollar purchases in the first seven months of this year to $38.1 billion. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  infuses cash into the system, when it buys dollars.   \par \par \uc2 Excess cash in the money market stokes price pressures and analysts expect that a soft inflation would provide the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more leeway to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's wholesale price inflation rate is forecast to ease to 3.27 percent for the 12 months to Sept. 8, a Reuters poll showed on Thursday. This would be its lowest level since December 2002. Inflation was 3.52 percent a week earlier.   \par \par \uc2 Cash with banks shrunk this week due to outflows of 350 billion rupees for tax payments by corporates.   \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-SWAPS|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070920e39k000sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
