\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Rises To New 9-Year High; Bonds Gain   \b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 September 2007\par 14:40\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest     Change \par  USD/INR           39.89      -0.32 \par  7.49% 2017 Bond   7.84%      -1 BP \par  Call Rate         7.00%      +70 BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par  August            0.68        -0.12 . \par *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose to its highest in nine years Thursday breaching a key level of INR40 to the dollar, on hopes that capital inflows will continue into the country after a U.S. Federal Reserve rate cut widened the interest rate differential in favor of the local unit.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR39.89, its lowest close since May 1998. It closed at INR40.42 Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said continued \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped stem further gains in the rupee, which hit an intraday low of INR39.86.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI has bought a reasonably good amount today but there are too many people waiting to dump (dollars)," said L. V. Prasad, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at  \uc2 IndusInd Bank.\par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained nearly 11% against the dollar this year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought $38 billion from the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market until July this year to stem the local unit's gains.   \par \par \uc2 "The local stock markets seem to be holding up. Also, with high oil prices, the RBI may not be too averse to letting the rupee rise," said Prasad.   \par \par \uc2 Local stocks ended at a record closing high, stretching a rally that saw the 30-stock Sensitive index breach 16,000 Wednesday.   \par \par \uc2 The Sensex gained 0.2% to end at 16,347.95.   \par \par \uc2 In the debt market, government bond prices rose on hopes of comfortable liquidity in the system as RBI's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is expected to bolster liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.49% 2017 paper closed at INR97.63 as against INR97.56 at its last close.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect bonds to take cues Friday from inflation data, due 0530GMT.   \par \par \uc2 India's inflation rate likely eased to 3.27% on year in the week ended Sept. 8, as against 3.52% in the previous week, as per a Dow Jones Newswires poll of five analysts.   \par \par \uc2 "Liquidity is set to improve, headline inflation is expected to go down further and (the economic) growth is showing signs of slowing down. The stage is set for a bond market rally," said the head of fixed income trading at a foreign bank, who didn't wish to be named..   \par \par \uc2 However, international crude oil prices remain a cause of concern, dealers added.   \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 20-09-07 1240GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070920e39k000wp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
