\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Indian rupee hits 9-yr high after Fed rate cut   \b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2007\par 14:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to fix headline format) (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 By V. Ramakrishnan   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Sept 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee hit a nine-year high on Wednesday as a sharp cut in interest rates by the U.S. Federal Reserve increased appetite for emerging market assets and a surging stock market attracted capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the rupee's gains were capped by heavy dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.20/21 per dollar, having risen to 40.18 during trade -- its highest since May 1998. The rupee gained more than half a percent from Tuesday's close of 40.48/49, and has risen more than 10 percent this year.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's previous high of 40.20 was hit in July.   \par \par \uc2 "Exporters got panicky and were selling their dollars throughout the day, and inflows are expected to be robust as evident by the soaring stock markets," said V. Soundarajan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at  \uc2 UCO Bank.\par \par \uc2 "I expect the rupee to break past the 40 per dollar mark before the end of this month," he said.   \par \par \uc2 The stock market <.BSESN> rose 4.2 percent, its biggest gain in 15 months, to a record-high close on hopes that the U.S. rate cut would help steady global credit markets and see foreigners return to emerging markets such as India.   \par \par \uc2 As well, Tuesday's cuts in U.S. interest rates raised India's interest rate premium over the United States to 300 basis points, which traders said would attract more capital inflows and add to the rupee's momentum.   \par \par \uc2 But those inflows complicate policy for the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the rupee rose this month and stepped in again as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  neared its highs.   \par \par \uc2 "They bought at every level. I think they are going to protect it," a chief dealer with a foreign bank said.   \par \par \uc2 A Reserve Bank of India spokeswoman said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not comment on the day-to-day movements on the exchange rate.   \par \par \uc2 Data this month showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $11.4 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in July, when the rupee was last near current levels, taking its dollar purchases in 2007 to 38.1 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve lowered its benchmark federal funds target rate by 50 basis points to 4.75 percent to shore up the world's largest economy against a housing slowdown and credit market turmoil. It also cut the discount rate it charges for direct loans to banks by a half-point to 5.25 percent.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 2, REPEAT)|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070919e39j002cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
