\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases taking cues from Asian stocks   \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2007\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 14 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased as traders were tentative after Asian stocks dipped on Tuesday, fuelling concerns that overseas investors would trim holdings in local equities amid weakening appetite for relatively risky assets.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m. (0415 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.66/67 per dollar, slightly off Monday's 40.625/635. It hit a nine-year high of 40.20 last month, with foreign buying of local stocks providing support.   \par \par \uc2 "It's a wait and watch game today, there's a fair amount of uncertainty at the moment," said a dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 Asian stocks succumbed to modest selling pressure following a negative lead from Wall Street, which put most of the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the defensive, despite nervousness over the dangers of a credit squeeze easing somewhat.   \par \par \uc2 Local traders said they would closely watch India's benchmark index <.BSESN> for cues about the rupee's direction.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign portfolio holdings stand at more than $9.6 billion this year despite sales since late July, compared with an inflow of $7.9 billion in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 Overseas investments in local stock have been a key support for the rupee, which has gained nearly 9 percent this year against the dollar, to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Still, the rupee's gains have been persistently capped by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and data on Monday showed the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $3.19 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, lower than $4.43 billion in May, to take its dollar purchases in 2007 to $26.7 billion.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -----------------------------------------------------------\par                   MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  ------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070817e38e0004x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
