\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Indian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says bought $3.19 bln in June   \b0\par\par\uc2 320 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2007\par 04:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats story issued late on Monday)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, Aug 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $3.19 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in June, lower than $4.43 billion in May, to take its dollar purchases this year to $26.7 billion, the Reserve Bank of India's monthly bulletin showed on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 Large capital inflows into Asia's third-biggest economy have complicated monetary management by pushing the rupee to nine-year highs against the dollar, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.   \par \par \uc2 After hitting a nine-year high of 40.28 per dollar in late May, the rupee <INR=IN> weakened to more than 41 per dollar in June and held above 40.50 per dollar for most of the month, lessening the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to have picked up again in July as a surge in the stock market to record highs drove the rupee to a new nine-year high of 40.20, traders and analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee's gains -- at its high it was up about 10 percent this year -- last week led to curbs on overseas borrowings by local firms and an increase in the amount of bonds the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  can issue to absorb funds generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Even after some selling since late July, foreign funds' net buying of Indian stocks stands at nearly $9.8 billion this year, higher than $7.39 billion in all of 2006 and just below a record of $10.7 billion in 2005.   \par \par \uc2 India's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves were a record $229.34 billion as at Aug. 3, up $52.1 billion so far in 2007 and the fifth-largest in Asia. Traders said a large part of that increase was due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INDIA\b0 \highlight\uc2 -CBANK/\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEAT)|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070814e38e0003e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
