\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 India \highlight\uc2  raises ceiling on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bonds - cbank   \b0\par\par\uc2 501 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 August 2007\par 04:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Repeats story issued late on Wednesday)  (Adds details, analyst comments and background)   \par \par \uc2  By V. Ramakrishnan   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, Aug 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  firepower on Wednesday, a day after it imposed limits on foreign borrowings by local firms in an effort to stem the strength of the rupee.   \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of India said the issue ceiling on bonds it can use to absorb funds generated by its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been raised to 1.5 trillion rupees ($37 billion) from 1.1 trillion rupees.   \par \par \uc2  The new ceiling for the fiscal year ending in March 2008 would be reviewed if outstanding issues of market stabilisation scheme (MSS) bonds exceeded 1.35 trillion rupees, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2  The outstanding balance of MSS bonds, including an auction held on Wednesday, was 989.7 billion rupees, it said.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the second increase in the ceiling this year -- it was previously raised in late April -- would give the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more control of the supply of cash in the money market, and that bond yields were likely to rise on Thursday. "The RBI itself has been surprised by the kind of liquidity," said Pradeep Madhav, chief operating officer at Securities Trading Corp of India.   \par \par \uc2  The RBI has bought billions of dollars to rein in the rupee, which, powered by foreign investment inflows, has risen about 10 percent against the dollar this year to nine-year highs, causing policy headaches.   \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  releases rupees into the local money market, which adds to inflationary pressures. To remove, or sterilise, the cash, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March resumed sales of MSS bonds.   \par \par \uc2  "To absorb the liquidity already infused, the increase in the ceiling on MSS will help," said S.P. Prabhu, head of trading at IDBI Gilts, adding tighter cash conditions would push bond yields up.   \par \par \uc2  "I expect the yield on the 10-year bond to rise 5 to 10 basis points tomorrow," he said.   \par \par \uc2  On July 31, the RBI raised reserve requirements for banks, a step it expects to remove $4 billion from the money market, and on Tuesday the government announced restrictions on local firms bringing foreign borrowings into the country.   \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Wednesday, Finance Minister Palaniappan Chidambaram had told Reuters that for now the government was not reviewing the ceiling on MSS bonds but would consider it if needed.   \par \par \uc2  Asia's third-largest economy grew by 9.4 percent in 2006/07, its fastest pace in 18 years, but the growth was accompanied by a surge in prices.   \par \par \uc2  Annual inflation hit a two-year high of 6.7 percent in late January, but has been below 5 percent since June.   \par \par \uc2  The RBI raised interest rates five times in 2006/07, most recently in late March.   \par \par \uc2  ($1=40.50 rupees)  (Additional reporting by Unni Krishnan in NEW DELHI and Anurag Joshi in MUMBAI)      \par \par \uc2 INDIA-ECONOMY/BONDS (UPDATE 1, REPEAT)|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070809e3890004b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
