\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee heads back towards 9-yr high on flows   \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juli 2007\par 05:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 26 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee headed back towards a nine-year high on Thursday, with the market shrugging off cues from other high-yielding Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that slipped against the dollar, in anticipation of strong capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m. (0415 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.31/32 per dollar, strengthening from the previous close of 40.3500/3575 and inching towards from a nine-year high of 40.20 hit earlier this week.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is looking for direction at the moment, and in the short run, its eyes are on the stock market," said a dealer with a foreign bank, who expects the rupee to trade in a 40.30-40.37 range on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Concerns over the fallout from the U.S. subprime market had abated slightly, and dealers built fresh positions in the rupee, expecting further appreciation.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee is the best performing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year, having gained nearly 10 percent in 2007, bolstered by robust investment flows into Asia's third largest economy.   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought more than $10.4 billion of stocks so far in 2007, edging towards a record $10.7 billion inflow in 2005 and higher than $8 billion in 2006.   \par \par \uc2 Still, dealers expected the rupee to trade in a narrow range, with gains limited by possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and firm prices of oil, \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest import.   \par \par \uc2 Oil prices <LCOc1> jumped on Wednesday after U.S. government data showed a draw in crude inventories as refiners stepped up runs to meet summer gasoline demand in the U.S., the world's top consumer.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070729e37q0001b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
