\par\par \b \uc2 India Rupee Hits New 9-Yr High On Foreign Fund Flows;Bonds Up   \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2007\par 15:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           40.29       -0.03 \par  7.49% 2017 Bond   7.74%       -7BPs \par  Call Rate         0.35%       +15BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    June            0.42        -0.17 . *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee rose to a new nine-year high against the U.S. dollar earlier Monday driven by strong foreign fund inflows to buy local stocks, before the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to rein in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR40.29 against INR40.32 at its close Friday. It touched an intraday low of INR40.22, a level last seen in May 1998.   \par \par \uc2 Most dealers expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow a gradual appreciation of the Indian unit.   \par \par \uc2 "The supply of dollars in the market is phenomenal, and it is the only the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  presence which is checking the slide for the dollar," said V. Rajagopal, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at  \uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank.\par \par \uc2 He expects the dollar to test INR40 by the end of the week as strong capital inflows from overseas investors persist, pushing local shares to new highs.   \par \par \uc2 Indian shares ended at an all-time high with the Bombay Stock Exchange's key 30-stock Sensex closing 1.1% higher at 15,732.20.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have bought over $9 billion worth of stocks so far in 2007, well over the $8 billion they bought in the previous year.   \par \par \uc2 In the bond market, Indian government bond prices rose as comfortable cash in the banking system and lower bond sales by the RBI spurred buying of securities, sending the benchmark 10-year yields to over five-and-a-half-month lows.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.49% 2017-dated bond ended at INR98.25, up from INR97.81 at the previous close.   \par \par \uc2 Its yield ended at 7.74%, down from 7.81% at Friday's close in India. It fell to 7.71% in intraday trade, the lowest yield for the 10-year paper since early February.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said lower-than-expected sales of bonds slated for the week by the RBI under the market stabilization scheme helped bonds gain.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI will sell INR20 billion of 7.55% 2010 bonds Wednesday under its market stabilization scheme to suck up excess liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 "We did see some profit-booking come in towards the close of trade but the general sentiment remains positive for bonds, given the ample liquidity in the system," said Namrata Padhye, fixed income analyst at IDBI Capital Markets.   \par \par \uc2 Government spending and persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have boosted rupee funds with banks, the biggest buyers of government debt. .   \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alpana Sarma [ 23-07-07 1302GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070723e37n0014g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
