\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Falls Below INR40.28, Lowest In 9 Years   \b0\par\par\uc2 695 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 2007\par 09:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The Indian rupee climbed to a new nine-year high against the U.S. dollar Monday, helped by strong foreign fund inflows into local stocks, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 At 0740GMT, the rupee was trading at 40.25 to a dollar, its highest intraday level against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 1998.   \par \par \uc2 "There are strong foreign fund inflows into the market, and we are also seeing some selling by banks on behalf of their corporate clients," a local bank dealer said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained about 9.5% against the dollar since January.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investors have bought over $9 billion worth of Indian stocks so far in 2007, well over the $8 billion they bought in the previous year.   \par \par \uc2 -By Vipin V. Nair; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; vipin.nair@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alpana Sarma [ 23-07-07 0749GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    (Updates an item ran at 0750GMT with more quotes, background) \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell to a new nine-year low against the Indian rupee Monday, as the rupee was boosted by strong foreign fund inflows, and some traders expect the dollar to go below the key INR40 barrier soon.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar's previous nine-year low was recorded on May 28 when it hit INR40.28.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1050GMT, the dollar was changing hands at INR40.29, up from INR40.22, its lowest level against the Indian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  since May 1998.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the dollar recovered due to the suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Reserve Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 India\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-owned banks.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "State-run banks have again come back to support the pair at 40.24. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , however, is not very heavy as the pair fell due to a one-off inflow," said a state-run bank dealer, who didn't wish to be named.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The rupee has gained about 9.5% against the dollar since January, mainly due to continuing foreign fund inflows, analysts said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Foreign investors have bought over $9 billion worth of Indian stocks so far in 2007, well over the $8 billion they bought in the previous year.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the dollar's global weakness also accentuated its fall in the local market.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar hit a record low versus the euro and a six-week low against the yen in Asia Monday on worries that problems in the U.S. subprime loan market could damage the broader economy.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to V. Rajagopal, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at Mumbai-based  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the dollar may fall further to test INR40.00 by Friday as strong capital inflows from overseas investors persist.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The supply of dollars in the market is phenomenal, and it is only the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  presence which is checking the slide for the dollar," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been regularly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in recent weeks to stem the rupee's sharp gains against the dollar.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of India bought $4.43 billion in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in May, up from $2.06 billion in April, according to lagged data available from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Exporters have been complaining that the rupee's gains have affected their profits.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Software companies  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Infosys Technologies\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500209.BY) and  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Satyam Computer Services\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500376.BY) recently lowered their earnings per share guidance for the current fiscal year due to the sharp gains in the rupee.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to R. K. Gurumoorthy, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at  \f28 \uc2 \f2 ING Vysya Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , though the rupee is poised to appreciate further in the near term, a widening trade deficit and rising crude oil prices could put pressure on it.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The biggest concern for the rupee is oil prices," he said.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Global crude oil prices are hovering around a 11-month high of $75.92 a barrel. India imports over 70% of its crude oil requirements.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's trade deficit in the January-March period widened to $15.232 billion from $11.752 billion in the year-ago quarter.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Vipin V. Nair; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 2288 4212; vipin.nair@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Alpana Sarma [ 23-07-07 1050GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020070723e37n000gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
