\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Gain On Lower Than Expected Inflation; Rupee Up   \b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juli 2007\par 15:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           40.32       -0.03 \par  7.49% 2017 Bond   7.81%       -2BPs \par  Call Rate         0.20%       +5BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    June            0.59        -0.08 . *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--Indian government bond prices rose Friday after a lower-than-expected inflation rate and comfortable liquidity led to buying in bonds.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Bonds prices, however, gave up some gains later in the session on Finance Minister P. Chidambaram's comments that the country's high economic growth is fueling inflation and current interest rates in the country are not unusually high.   \par \par \uc2 The most actively traded 7.49% 2017 bond ended at INR97.81 against INR97.63 at the last close.   \par \par \uc2 Market participants said dealers also pared positions later in the session expecting the RBI to sell bonds next week under its market stabilization scheme to suck out excess liquidity.   \par \par \uc2 The inflation rate was 4.27% on year for week ended July 7, unchanged over previous week, but lower than an estimated average of 4.32% of seven economists polled by Dow Jones Newswires.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI estimates inflation to be close to 5% in the current financial year that began April 1.   \par \par \uc2 "When it raises rates, inflation comes down but at an appropriate time it can revisit the rates," Chidambaram said.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI will meet July 31 to review monetary policy and most market participants expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hold interest rates steady.   \par \par \uc2 The cutoffs at a federal bond auction came in line with market estimates.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI sold INR60 billion of 7.27% 2013 bond and INR30 billion of 7.95% 2032 bond.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the Indian rupee inched closer to its nine-year highs, but strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  staved off further gains.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar ended at INR40.32 as against INR40.35 at the last close.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  protected the dollar throughout the session, in the face of strong foreign fund inflows.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI is on one side and the market is on the other side," said a foreign bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect the rupee to trade in a tight range unless the RBI budges from current levels.   \par \par \uc2 "They (RBI) have bought a reasonably good amount today. They will try to protect this level next week," said L.V. Prasad, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at  \uc2 IndusInd Bank.\par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India has bought $4.426 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in May. In the fiscal year that ended March 31, the RBI bought $26.824 billion. .   \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Alpana Sarma [ 20-07-07 1332GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070720e37k000qo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
