\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee eases as oil firms step up dlr buying   \b0\par\par\uc2 313 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2007\par 04:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 19 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee slipped on Thursday as rising oil prices spurred oil companies to buy dollars, though dealers expected capital flows into the fast-growing economy to bolster the local unit.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:45 a.m. (0415 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.43/44 per dollar, easing from Wednesday's 40.4150/4250, and drifting further from a nine-year peak of 40.28 hit in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "Oil companies have called the shots in the morning, but trading has been subdued, and most of the market is looking for direction," said a senior dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 A fall in U.S. gasoline stocks pushed up oil prices to above $76 a barrel <LCOc1>. Oil is India's largest import.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the prospect of strong foreign fund flows, specifically into local equities, limited the rupee's losses, with a section of the market building fresh positions in the local unit on expectations of a renewed burst of capital inflows.   \par \par \uc2 The spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed over the market, though the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not seen buying dollars in early trade, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely believed to have bought dollars recently to keep a lid on the rupee, which has gained about 9.5 percent against the dollar in 2007 to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee's rise has dented the profits of Indian exporters, and India's third-largest software services exporter, Wipro , said on Thursday that the rupee's rise had an impact of 3.4 percent on April-June margins.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070722e37j0001d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
