\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-India's easy overnight rate not a policy signal   \b0\par\par\uc2 By V. Ramakrishnan and Saikat Chatterjee   \par \uc2 825 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2007\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 18 (Reuters) - Capital inflows and government spending have kept India's overnight rates below the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lending rate for more than a month, but no one expects a cut when the Reserve Bank of India reviews policy on July 31.   \par \par \uc2 Overnight cash rates that are lower than a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rates can often suggest pressure to lower the official rates.   \par \par \uc2 But Indian overnight money below 1 percent signals that policymakers are less worried that extra cash in circulation will stoke inflation, and means they could hold rates steady this time.   \par \par \uc2 After five rate increases between June 2006 and March this year, annual inflation has slowed from a two-year high of 6.7 percent in January to just above 4 percent at the end of June.   \par \par \uc2 As a result, the RBI has switched from containing inflation to containing rupee strength, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from breaching a nine-year high of 40.28 per dollar <INR=IN> set in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "Last year inflation had become a critical problem, now the rupee is more of an issue," said A. Prasanna, an analyst with ICICI Securities in Mumbai.   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI has achieved what it wanted -- now the focus is on the rupee."   \par \par \uc2 Overnight money rates <INROND=>, the rate at which commercial banks lend to each other, are a barometer of cash supplies in the banking system. At 0.10-1.0 percent, they are far below the 7.75 percent at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lends to the market.   \par \par \uc2 Much of the supply has come from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to absorb foreign funds flows into \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's record-breaking stock market.   \par \par \uc2 Foreign investments into local stocks total a net $8.4 billion so far this year, more than the $7.9 billion for all 2006, and in May alone the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the tune of $4.4 billion, taking total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2007 to $23.4 billion.   \par \par \uc2 When it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buys dollars and sells rupees, which enter the banking system. It often sterilises these potentially inflationary sales by issuing special bonds, but these incur interest and analysts say issuance has not kept pace with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because policy-makers want to keep costs down.   \par \par \uc2 "Right now inflation is not high and you can allow some liquidity to come back into the market," said V. Anantha Nageswaran, head of investment research at  \uc2 Bank Julius Baer\uc2  in Singapore.   \par \par \uc2 WILD MOVEMENTS   \par \par \uc2 Prasanna at ICICI Securities said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be going slow on issuing \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds because the cap is 1.1 trillion rupees ($27.23 billion), and it has already issued 802 billion rupees worth. It may also want to keep some firepower in case inflation or rupee pressures build later in the year.   \par \par \uc2 Others say rupee pressure is likely to ease later this year as capital inflows ease and oil refiners step up dollar buying to keep pace with rising global oil prices.   \par \par \uc2 But if pressure does continue, the RBI could raise banks' reserve requirements to reduce lendable resources -- a step it took three times between December and the end of March.   \par \par \uc2 Rajeev Malik, an economist at  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  in Singapore, said persistently easy cash has led some to expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shift from a tightening stance to a neutral stance.   \par \par \uc2 "We think these expectations are optimistic," Malik said. "Although we expect no more repo (lending) rate hikes, it is too early to signal lower policy rates."   \par \par \uc2 Although wholesale price inflation, the most widely watched price indicator, is within the RBI's 5 percent comfort zone, money supply is still above target and the property and stock markets remain hot. Only loan growth has shown signs of cooling.   \par \par \uc2 Short-term borrowing by the government from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  topped 300 billion rupees in early July, reflecting higher spending, and analysts say this is also boosting cash supplies.   \par \par \uc2 But Malik said this could be transitory, with the government front-loading its spending for the fiscal year which began in April, and with less \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as capital flows ease.   \par \par \uc2 Overnight rates have swung wildly, hitting a 10-year high of 70 percent in March and a decade low of 0.10 percent in June.   \par \par \uc2 ICICI Securities' Prasanna said rates would stabilise if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  removed a 30 billion rupee cap at its daily borrowing window, which limits how much it can drain from the market. Lifting the cap would incur higher costs for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Prasanna said keeping it risked sending wrong signals.   \par \par \uc2 "If this continues for some more time, banks will likely take it as a signal that things have eased," he said.   \par \par \uc2 "Deposit rates will ease and so will lending rates and then there will be a dilution of the policy stance."   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RATES/ (ANALYSIS)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|ABX   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070721e37i000md\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
