\par\par \b \uc2 Indian Corporate Debt-Issues pick up as rates seen steady   \b0\par\par\uc2 414 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2007\par 11:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 17 (Reuters) - Indian firms are expected to step up fund raising this week as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to leave rates unchanged in its policy review on July 31, merchant bankers said.   \par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll of 11 economists last week showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to hold its key rates steady at its July 31 policy review. For story, double-click [ID:nBOM294664].   \par \par \uc2 "Steady rates would bring bond yields down and also narrow spreads between sovereign and corporate bonds," the merchant banking head with a private bank said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said ample cash supplies in the banking system and expectations of inflation remaining within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone have also helped sentiment for corporate bonds.   \par \par \uc2 Cash supplies have risen mainly because of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to check the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 Data on Monday showed the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) bought $4.4 billion in May, taking its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of November 2006 to $28.4 billion.   \par \par \uc2 India's wholesale price inflation was at 4.27 percent in the 12 months to June 30, down from a two-year high of 6.7 percent in January and within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's medium-term target of 4.0-4.5 percent.   \par \par \uc2 State-run Bank of India <BOI> raised 4 billion rupees through a perpetual bond sale, which opened and closed on Monday.  \uc2 Punjab National Bank\uc2  sold perpetual bonds worth 5 billion rupees last week.   \par \par \uc2 State-run Bank of Maharashtra raised 2 billion rupees via an Upper Tier II bond issue, which opened last week.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, state-run refiner  \uc2 Indian Oil Corp\uc2  sold oil bonds worth 28.5 billion rupees. The government issued IOC these bonds to compensate it for selling retail fuel below market prices.   \par \par \uc2 The yield on Reuters' benchmark 5-year corporate paper <AAAIN5Y=> was at 9.35 percent on Tuesday, lower than 9.60 percent a week ago.   \par \par \uc2 The spread between the 5-year corporate paper and government debt stood at about 161 basis points <0#AAAINBMK=>, narrower from 187 a week back.   \par \par \uc2 Corporate debt pages on Reuters: <INCORP02>-<INCORP-05>   \par \par \uc2 Spreads over federal bonds <0#AAAINBMK=>   \par \par \uc2 Commercial paper placements <IN/CREDENCE>   \par \par \uc2 Secondary market CP Prices <INCP01>   \par \par \uc2 Secondary market bond prices <0#INBOND=>   \par \par \uc2 Inter-corporate deposits <INCRED13>   \par \par \uc2 Recent ratings <IN/CREDENCE>   \par \par \uc2 Corporate bond yield curve <0#AAAINBMK=> <INCRED10>   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-CORPDEBT/|LANGEN|SNI|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070717e37h000oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
