\par\par \b \uc2 India Bonds Gain Amid Ample Liquidity; Rupee Up   \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2007\par 15:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                    As Of 1200 GMT \par                    Latest      Change \par  USD/INR           40.37       -0.06 \par  7.49% 2017 Bond   7.90%       -3BPs \par  Call Rate         0.40%       -10BPs \par  Forward Dollar Premium/Discount* \par    June            0.72       -0.03 . *Forward Dollar Premium/Discount is midpoint of bid-offer spreads. \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUMBAI (Dow Jones)--India government bond prices rose Monday as traders drew comfort from ample system liquidity and ignored a slew of bond and treasury bill sales slated for the week.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dealers expect bond prices to remain firm in the coming sessions in the likely absence of any monetary action by the RBI before its mid-term review July 31.   \par \par \uc2 The benchmark 7.49% 2017 bond closed at INR97.18 as against INR96.99 at the last close.   \par \par \uc2 "The current liquidity surplus in the banking system should offset the planned bond sales this week, and with the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, more liquidity is being injected," said Arun Kaul, treasurer at  \uc2 Punjab National Bank.\uc2 Kotak Mahindra Bank\uc2 , in a note to clients, pegs inflows during the week at INR127.06 billion, primarily on account of coupon payments and redemptions of state development loans.   \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, the rupee rose close to nine-year highs, but further gains were thwarted by RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "The RBI has been protecting the dollar at INR40.28-INR40.30 levels. It is however not trying to reverse the rupee appreciation trend as the nature of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shows," said a private bank dealer.   \par \par \uc2 The RBI bought $4.426 billion in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in May, lagged \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is trying to find out when the RBI will move away. However, it is not in a mood to challenge the RBI as seen by the short covering whenever the RBI \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the dealer added.   \par \par \uc2 He expects the dollar to trade in a INR40.30-INR40.45 band Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 -By Subhadip Sircar; Dow Jones Newswires; 91 22 22884212; djn.in@dowjones.com [ 16-07-07 1322GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 1164 1847 62506   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020070716e37g000mg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
