\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee gains as stocks hit record high   \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juli 2007\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 13 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee strengthened on Friday as foreign money poured into the record-setting stock market, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to cap the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength, traders said.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.42/43 per dollar, up from the previous close of 40.50/40.51.   \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is making little difference as foreign inflows continue to be high," a trader at a state-run bank said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars between 40.42 and 40.45 levels.   \par \par \uc2 India's main share index <.BSESN> hit its eighth record high in 10 sessions on Friday, before ending up 1.2 percent at a record close. For story, click on: [ID:nBOM248058].   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought $1.9 billion of equities in the first eight days of July, taking their total purchases this year to $7.6 billion -- almost equal to total foreign buying of $7.9 billion for all of last year. On Thursday, the rupee came close to testing a nine-year high of 40.28 hit in May, but aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  pushed it down to a two-week low of 40.75.   \par \par \uc2 Strong economic growth and buoyant stocks have attracted capital inflows, sending the rupee up by about 9.5 percent so far in 2007. This has hurt exporters' margins and forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the rupee's rise.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $2.1 billion through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, taking the total purchases to $24 billion in the six months to end-April.   \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the government unveiled a $320 million relief package for exporters hurt by the rupee's rise.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070716e37d0004d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
