\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee falls, heavy cbank hand seen   \b0\par\par\uc2 381 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2007\par 05:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to afternoon)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 12 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee backed away from a recent 9-year high, falling by as much as 1 percent against the dollar on Thursday, with dealers citing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the key factor.   \par \par \uc2 At 2:12 p.m. (0842 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.54/551 per dollar, after falling to a two-week low of 40.75 from a high of 40.33 in the morning.   \par \par \uc2 It closed at 40.40/41 on Wednesday, and had hit a nine-year high of 40.28 per dollar in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) came in very aggressively around the 40.35-40.40 levels and kicked (dollar/rupee) higher," said a local trader.   \par \par \uc2 "The market was forced to cut back on its heavy short-dollar bets," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought around $200-$400 million.   \par \par \uc2 "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) does not comment on the day to day movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought $2.06 billion through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in April, taking its total purchases to $24 billion for the six months from November.   \par \par \uc2 It is widely suspected of selling rupees over the past month to keep the dollar above 40 rupees.   \par \par \uc2 Heavy capital inflows have pushed the rupee up by about 9 percent so far in 2007, making it Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to protect exporters' margins.   \par \par \uc2 Infosys Technologies\uc2  , \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 's number-two software exporter, on Wednesday cut its full-year earnings forecast in rupee terms and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp rise was hurting its operating margins.   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought Indian shares worth more than $7.5 billion so far in 2007, compared with $8 billion for the whole of 2006.   \par \par \uc2 RBI Governor Yaga Venugopal Reddy said earlier this month the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was facing severe policy challenges in managing capital flows and analysts expect overseas borrowings to be tightened to help curb inflows.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par  -----------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070715e37c0001c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
