\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee edges towards 9-yr peak, cbank watched   \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2007\par 04:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 10 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee edged towards a nine-year peak on Tuesday, driven up by moderate investment flows, but the gains were limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and dollar purchases by an oil importer, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.3950/4050 per dollar, up from Monday's 40.425/44, and inching within sight of a nine-year peak of 40.28 hit in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "The fact that we closed below 40.40 is quite significant -- it's a level the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been defending in recent days," said a dealer with a private bank.   \par \par \uc2 "The market is likely to take that as a sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may tolerate further rupee appreciation," the dealer added.   \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars as the rupee approached its intraday peak of 40.37.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely thought to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent sharp spurts in the rupee, which, with a gain of about 9.5 percent, is Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar this year.   \par \par \uc2 India's main share index <.BSESN> hit a lifetime high for the seventh session in a row on Tuesday, boosting sentiment for the rupee on expected foreign inflows, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 Foreigners have bought $7.4 billion of local equities this year, including $1.7 billion in the first six trading days of July.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers expressed some caution about oil prices <LCOc1>, which were trading near 11-month highs. Oil is India's largest import so a large and sustained rise that inflated India's import bill could weigh on the rupee.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -----------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index         <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)              <INR=IN>\par   -----------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|RBN|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070713e37a0004a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
