\par\par \b \uc2 TRADE IDEA-Indian rupee may rise more-Bank America   \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2007\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 5 (Reuters) -  \uc2 Bank of America\uc2  recommends buying the partially convertible Indian rupee <INR=IN> as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may take measures to drain cash from the banking system that, in turn, could push up interest rates.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in recent months, had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to check the rupee's rise against the U.S. dollar, but also had to drain the excess cash resulting from its move.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of India thus increased banks' cash reserve requirements three times since December and sold market stabilisation bonds from March until a month ago.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has risen by more than 9 percent in 2007 making it Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Overnight money rates <INROND=> -- an indicator of cash surpluses __ has fallen to 0.30 percent, nearing a 10-year low of 0.10 percent hit in June and below 0.50-0.75 percent on Wednesday due to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) was again spotted on Thursday selling rupees around the 40.45 per dollar mark.   \par \par \uc2 But Hans-Sia Yeo and Lawrence Goodman, analysts at  \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , said a prolonged continuation of easy cash may blunt the RBI's objective of maintaining a tight policy stance.   \par \par \uc2 "We expect the RBI to tighten liquidity conditions in coming weeks, either via higher sterilisation bond issuances in coming weeks or another 0.5 percent increase in the cash reserve ratio," it said in a note on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 A reluctance by the authorities to impose capital controls and estimated equity-related capital inflows worth around 30 billion rupees in June and July would underpin the rupee's gains, it said.   \par \par \uc2 "We recommend establishing a short dollar/rupee position, expressed via a 1-month non-deliverable forward at 40.54 <INR1MNDFOR=>. We target to take profit at 39.14, with a stop on two-day close above the 41 figure," it said.   \par \par \uc2 It was at 40.50 on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 INDIA-RUPEE/ (TRADEIDEA)|LANGEN|SNI   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070705e375000vt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
