\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee climbs to 1-mth high on flow outlook   \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2007\par 04:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2  MUMBAI, July 3 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee rose to its highest level in a month on Tuesday, spurred by the prospect of surging investment flows into Asia's third-largest economy.   \par \par \uc2  At 9:50 a.m. (0420 GMT), the rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.54/55 per dollar, its highest since June 6, and strengthening from Monday's 40.65/66.   \par \par \uc2  "The positive signals from Asian equities are leading the market to believe that the stock market will do well, and that the inflows will be good," said the chief dealer with a foreign bank, who is expecting the rupee to trade in a 40.52-40.62 range on Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2  The dealer said the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  was likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 40.52 to cap the rupee's gains.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee has been trading in a 40.50-41.25 range since early May, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely suspected of buying dollars to keep the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weaker than 40.50, though over the last three weeks it was seen ensuring the rupee did not firm beyond 40.70.   \par \par \uc2  The rupee hit a nine-year high of 40.28 in late May, but was knocked off its peak by suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has gained about 9 percent this year, driven higher by robust capital flows into the fast-growing economy.   \par \par \uc2  Foreign funds have poured $5.7 billion into Indian equities this year, after investing about $8 billion in 2006.   \par \par \uc2  A Reuters survey of 11 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists conducted on June 29 showed the market was slightly more positive on the rupee, compared with the middle of June, extending the rupee-bullish view the market has held for most of this year. For related story, please double-click on [ID:nSP38076].    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   -------------------------------------------------------------\par                     MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          .BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               INR=IN>\par  --------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE/ (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070706e3730003z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
