\par\par \b \uc2 India bond yields end lower on easy cash conditions   \b0\par\par\uc2 268 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2007\par 05:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, July 3 (Reuters) - Indian 10-year bond yields fell to a one-month low on Tuesday as traders took advantage of ample cash supplies to buy debt, but there was an expectation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may try to drain funds from the market.   \par \par \uc2 The yield on the 10-year federal bond <IN074917G=CC> ended at 8.09 percent, down from the previous close of 8.11 percent. The yield eased as far as 8.08 percent during trade, the lowest since early June.   \par \par \uc2 There were inflows of about 45 billion ($1.1 billion) into the banking system due to bond coupon payments over the weekend, and other funds came in from suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said.   \par \par \uc2 Reflecting the easy cash conditions, overnight interest rates <INROND=> fell to 1.25-1.30 percent from 2.50 percent on Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  received 395 billion rupees of bids in its afternoon reverse repo auction.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step up sale of market stabilisation bonds in the coming days to drain cash," a foreign bank trader said.   \par \par \uc2 Market stabilisation bonds can be used to absorb rupees released into the system when the RBI buys dollars to cap the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday, when the rupee strengthened past the 40.50 per dollar.    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par \