\par\par \b \uc2 Indian rupee steady as traders await fresh triggers   \b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2007\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to open)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee was steady on Friday as expectations of robust capital inflows were offset by demand for dollars from oil refiners and the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem its rise, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 At 9:50 a.m. (0420 GMT), the partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> was at 40.71/72 per dollar, unchanged from Thursday's close. It has been trading in a 40.50-41.25 range since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked it from a nine-year high of 40.28 in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "The flow position looks good, the question is whether the rupee is allowed to move up once the natural resistance in the form of oil demand peters out later today," said a dealer with a foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee below 40.50 since end-May, but has been widely suspected of selling rupees every time it tests 40.70 over the past week, perhaps indicating a lower tolerance level for the local unit's strength, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained about 8.5 percent against the dollar this year, to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, driven higher by strong foreign investment flows.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said foreign investor demand for a $2.1 billion domestic share sale by ICICI Bank had underpinned the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 The relatively high yielding Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also been a favourite with carry traders, who sell low-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the yen in favour of high-yielding assets like the rupee.   \par \par \uc2 Still, robust demand for dollars by oil refiners blocked the rupee, dealers said. Oil prices <LCOc1> steadied above $70 a barrel as a strike continued in the world's eighth-largest producer Nigeria.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Oil is India's largest import.  \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|SNI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070625e36m0003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
