\par\par \b \uc2 India rupee eases on oil as dealers search for cues   \b0\par\par\uc2 299 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2007\par 04:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Updates to close)   \par \par \uc2 MUMBAI, June 22 (Reuters) - The Indian rupee eased on Friday, after trading in a narrow band for most of the session, driven lower by dollar purchases by oil refiners and as dealers unwound positions in the local unit ahead of the weekend. The partially convertible rupee <INR=IN> ended at 40.77/78 per dollar from Thursday's 40.71/72. It has been trading in a 40.50-41.25 range since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  knocked it from a nine-year high of 40.28 in late May.   \par \par \uc2 "There wasn't much happening today, looks like the market is resigned to trading within a band for the time being," said a dealer with a foreign bank.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that state-run banks were seen buying dollars when the rupee moved towards its intraday peak of 40.69, though the market was unsure if the purchases were on behalf of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 India\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBI) has been suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the rupee below 40.50 since end-May, but has been widely suspected of selling rupees every time it tests 40.70 over the past week, perhaps indicating a lower tolerance level for the local unit's strength, dealers said.   \par \par \uc2 The rupee has gained about 8.5 percent against the dollar this year, to be Asia's best performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , driven higher by strong foreign investment flows.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said foreign investor demand for a $2.1 billion domestic share sale by ICICI Bank had    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par underpinned the rupee.  \par ---------------------------------------------------------------\par                    MARKET SNAPSHOT\par  Bombay Sensitive Index          <.BSESN>\par  Indian rupee (/$)               <INR=IN>\par  ---------------------------------------------------------------\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-INDIA-RUPEE (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|Table|SNI|ABN|M|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020070625e36m0003v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
